Hello,

I've checked another cluster and I confirm there's an issue, but it's not related to the indicator itself but the way we retrieve the settings from the cluster. Evidence:

1. Within the cluster, getting the values, I can confirm they are correctly defined:
```
GET _cluster/settings?&include_defaults=true&filter_path=*.cluster.max_shards_per_node*
{
  "persistent": {
    "cluster": {
      "max_shards_per_node": "1500"
    }
  },
  "defaults": {
    "cluster": {
      "max_shards_per_node": {
        "frozen": "3000"
      }
    }
  }
}
```
But when fetching the indicator, we got:

```
GET _health_report/shards_capacity
{
  "cluster_name": "96b3ed3d4d6b4fbe83a793d9ed6debee",
  "indicators": {
    "shards_capacity": {
      "status": "red",
      "symptom": "Cluster is close to reaching the configured maximum number of shards for data nodes.",
      "details": {
        "data": {
          "max_shards_in_cluster": 7000,
          "current_used_shards": 7054
        },
        "frozen": {
          "max_shards_in_cluster": 0
        }
      },
      "impacts": [
        {
          "id": "elasticsearch:health:shards_capacity:impact:upgrade_blocked",
          "severity": 1,
          "description": "The cluster has too many used shards to be able to upgrade.",
          "impact_areas": [
            "deployment_management"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "elasticsearch:health:shards_capacity:impact:creation_of_new_indices_blocked",
          "severity": 1,
          "description": "The cluster is running low on room to add new shards. Adding data to new indices is at risk",
          "impact_areas": [
            "ingest"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "diagnosis": [
        {
          "id": "elasticsearch:health:shards_capacity:diagnosis:increase_max_shards_per_node",
          "cause": "Elasticsearch is about to reach the maximum number of shards it can host, based on your current settings.",
          "action": "Increase the value of [cluster.max_shards_per_node] cluster setting or remove data indices to clear up resources.",
          "help_url": "https://ela.st/fix-shards-capacity"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

in this case, the cluster has 7 data nodes, and the value of `"max_shards_in_cluster": 7000 (=7 * 1000)` matches with the setting configured to 1000 (the default value). After checking different things I did update the setting to `1500` and the indicator switched to green, with `"max_shards_in_cluster": 10500 (= 7 * 1500)`, so the indicator is working as expected, but _something_ is not happening with the setting retrieval. I'll close this ticket and create a new issue with this information.
